entry.summary:
Imagine You're Standing Outside a Shop... Have you ever noticed something interesting when you walk past a shop? Even before entering, you can see the shop's name board. "Fresh Mart" You don't need to enter the shop to know its name. It's visible to everyone from outside. But what about the products? Can you see all the products from outside? No. To access products, you must enter the shop. Now let's connect this simple real-world example to Java. Imagine this Java class: public class Shop {
static int age = 20; static String name = "Fresh Mart";
String prod_name; }
Think of it this way:
Shop Story Java Concept
Shop building Class
Shop name board Static variable
Product inside shop Non-static variable
Entering the shop Creating an object
